--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 4080770848284654832da6e1e1aff82a, type: 3}
  m_Name: WharfLighting
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: HiddenHarbours.World::HiddenHarbours.World.WharfLightingDef
  Id: lighting.stp_wharf
  DisplayName: St Peters wharf
  LanternSites: []
  LanternsCastShadows: 1
  LanternIntensityScale: 2.5
  LanternReachMetres: 7.5
  LitPoleIds: []
  PolesCastShadows: 1
  PoleIntensityScale: 1
  PoleReachMetres: 7
  MarkerBloomMetres: 1
  MarkerIntensity: 1.6
  MarkerEdgeSoftness: 0.6
  WestGreen: {r: 0.3, g: 1, b: 0.5, a: 1}
  EastRed: {r: 1, g: 0.22, b: 0.15, a: 1}
  HarbourMarkIds:
  - channel.stpeters_entrance.s3
  - channel.stpeters_entrance.p3
  HarbourMarkerLook: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 6540e0ec029b4217a6863baec4460b19, type: 2}
  LanternsWithoutShadows:
  - lanternPost_0
  Why: 'St Peters'' two pier lanterns burned at the shared lantern preset, which left the deck near black at night once Nine Mile Creek''s wharf was brought up to a readable night. They now burn 2.5 times the preset with a 7.5 m pool, the same as Nine Mile Creek''s wall lanterns. The preset itself is untouched: every doorstep and lane lantern in the village uses it. The sites stay where the pier''s own layout puts them (StPetersWharf.LampPostSites): one at the head and one at the root, with the middle left dark on purpose (municipal-infrastructure.md 3.4). The red and green off the pier head are the entrance channel''s inner pair (s3, p3); they wear the harbour-marker look (a small glass core, a soft low halo, lens colours, a faint streak on the water) instead of the coast-wide nav preset, which every other mark keeps. The head lantern throws no lamp shadows: the red can stands 4 m off it and the shadow system threw her silhouette 6 m across open water as a dark spike. The root lantern still casts. The marker values above (MarkerBloom and the head colours) are for breakwater lights and are unused here.'
